{
 "about": "Rule from a search's product category (eval/queries.json `category`) to the place tags that let a classifier say 'plausibly sells it' from the tag alone. `yes`: the tag names a shop type that stocks the product as a matter of course. `weak`: a general merchant that may stock it (department, variety, discount, supermarket, drugstore, farm store). Anything else, or no shop/amenity/craft tag at all, is `no`. OSM entries are `key=value` over shop, amenity and craft; Overture entries are matched against any element of taxonomy.hierarchy (which includes taxonomy.primary) and against basic_category. The Overture lists were aligned to the vocabulary seen in the raw Overture rows (basic_category and taxonomy.primary values) before the match step ran; two consistency fixes were made after a first look at the OSM matches (README.md, Run notes).",
